,"files_count":77,"item_last_updated":1625312998,"item_size":1866822173,"metadata":{"identifier":"wonder_jet_TNA","title":"Wonder Jet","mediatype":"movies","collection":["british_gov_public_films","ephemera"],"subject":"jet propulsion; Frank Whittle","description":"Behind the jet engine of today lies a story of British pioneering. The development of the jet propulsion gas-turbine. jet engine. Air Commodore Sir Frank Whittle.  Power Jet W.1.","date":"1950","hidden":"true","publicdate":"2005-10-07 10:37:26","addeddate":"2005-10-07 17:36:46","uploader":"florian@archive.org","sponsor":"Central Office of Information for Ministry of Supply","publisher":"Crown Film Unit","sound":"sound","color":"color","runtime":"19:14","credits":"Public Information Films","rights":"UK Crown Copyright","language":"english","coverage":"Great Britain","updatedate":"2005-10-07 10:39:42","updater":"nVIR","backup_location":"ia903600_10","ia_orig__runtime":"19 Minutes 14 Seconds"},"reviews":[{"reviewbody":"Fairly interesting, if a bit pedestrian and badly acted, but also rather bizarre at times (e.g. contrasting the people developing the jet engine with the local gentry out fox-hunting). To be honest, it's probably more interesting for what it shows of British life in the 50s than the development of the jet engine!","reviewtitle":"Weird or wonder?","stars":"3","reviewer":"movieman","createdate":"2005-11-27 07:03:57","reviewdate":"2005-11-27 07:03:57"},{"reviewbody":"Never mind the acting, or the fox hunters.It is a good primer for those who know nothing about jet engines. And, an interesting film for an engineer like myself who knows jet engines.","reviewtitle":"For the engineer","stars":"4","reviewer":"R. Freedman","createdate":"2006-02-24 13:25:07","reviewdate":"2006-02-24 13:25:07"},{"reviewbody":"Odd that they concentrate on Leicestershire and show a Coventry (three spires) skyline, without mentioning his Coventrian roots. As a son of Coventry I'm a trifle piqued. Ho-Hum, said Pooh. Check this out http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank_Whittle#In_Whittle.27s_birthplace.2C_Coventry.2C_England.2C_UK\n\nI believe there's a plaque in his honour on Hearsal common.\n\n2007 snogs","reviewtitle":"A Coventry Hero!","reviewer":"SirJekyllAppliance","reviewdate":"2007-10-31 14:07:43","createdate":"2007-10-31 14:07:43","stars":"3"},{"reviewbody":"Fun little film, told newsreel style, about the advent of the jet engine. Curious images abound, especially in the beginning, but I guess it does it's job, because it certainly kept my interest. ","reviewtitle":"THE GAS TURBINE IS NOW BRITAIN'S ROSPERITY ","reviewer":"Spuzz","reviewdate":"2008-06-20 00:45:22","createdate":"2008-06-20 00:45:22","stars":"4"}],"server":"dn800208.us.archive.org","simplelists":{"solo_manifest":{"solo_manifest_dn800208":{"sys_changed_by":{"source":"task","task_id":"5428838780"},"sys_last_changed":"2026-06-10 14:31:56.269913"}}},"solo":true,"uniq":516120904,"workable_servers":["dn800208.us.archive.org"]}